  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was solid execution across the board\u2014Port Washington posted 5% grooming growth on core grooms despite add-on attach dropping from 55% to 41%, and Hicksville delivered 36% grooming growth with a 33% transaction lift. The real story: you're running 14% more groomer-days MTD at Port Washington versus last month while maintaining near-baseline productivity ($478 vs $505/groomer-day), which signals the new capacity is absorbing volume efficiently. YTD, you're up 45% revenue and appointments\u2014that's structural momentum worth tracking.\n\nHowever, there's a pattern worth your attention. Retail collapsed at both stores\u2014Port Washington down 25%, Hicksville down 77%\u2014while grooming and add-ons held or improved. This isn't inventory: you're only 20 SKUs out at each location, none critical. This smells like front-of-house execution or customer traffic timing; the team isn't upselling retail during the groom transaction. Separately, Hicksville's $/groomer-day ($348 vs $407 baseline) is underperforming by 15%, signaling either lower-priced bookings, scheduling inefficiency, or idle time on the 4-groomer schedule. Port Washington's add-on attach decline also warrants a check-in\u2014that's a 14-point drop and doesn't track with volume gains.\n\nMonth-to-date, both stores beat DOW-adjusted expectations (Port +6.5%, Hicksville +8.4%), so the calendar isn't headwind. Lapse pools total $388K combined annual value\u2014meaningful reactivation runway if you want it. Reorder critical items: X-Small Treat Table (negative stock at both locations), Shanti's Medical Journey, and bully sticks.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Today 6 groomer-days Port / 4 Hicksville (10 total, 14.0 bather hours combined); tomorrow 7 Port / 4 Hicksville (11 total, 14.0h); next 7 days 38 Port / 18 Hicksville (56 total groomer-days)."
